### Use "lsusb" in terminal to identify devices
### Example:
### Bus 001 Device 009: ID 37b0:0040 LAMZU Thorn V2
### "37b0" is the vendor ID and "0040" is the product ID

# Lamzu Thorn V2 Wired
# Bus 001 Device 009: ID 37b0:0040 LAMZU Thorn V2

# Lamzu Thorn V2 Wired DFU
# Bus 001 Device 031: ID 37b0:0041 LAMZU LAMZU THORN V2 DFU

# Lamzu Thorn V2 Dongle
# Bus 001 Device 026: ID 37b0:002e LAMZU LAMZU 8K Dongle V2 Dongle

# Lamzu Thorn V2 Dongle DFU
# Bus 001 Device 029: ID 37b0:0033 LAMZU LAMZU THORN V2 8K Dongle DFU

# Should not need these
# KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="37b0", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0041", MODE="0666", TAG+="uaccess"
# KERNEL=="hidraw*", ATTRS{idVendor}=="37b0", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0033", MODE="0666", TAG+="uaccess"

### How to update firmware on Linux
# Use Chrome based browser
# Go to lamzu.net
# Click "Firmware Update"
# Click "Update""
# Click "Check Current Firmware Version"
# Select the correct HID device in the browser prompt
# Click "Upgrade" and the device will go into DFU mode but fail to prompt to connect the DFU device
# Go into DevTools (F12) and run this in console:
# await navigator.hid.requestDevice({ filters: [{ vendorId: 0x37b0 }] })
# Browser should now show a prompt to connect the DFU device
